  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shyamveer vs State Of U.P. on 18 September, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 78 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 37305 of 2019 Applicant :- Shyamveer Opposite Party :- State Of U.P.",
    "facts": "Offence under section 60 (1)/63 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 01.08.2019, who is not a previous convict.",
    "arguments": "The submission is that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under sections272, 420, 467, 468 and 471I.P.C. is unjustified. Learned A.G.A. opposed the prayer for bail but could not dispute the aforesaid facts as argued by learned counsel for the applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The submission is that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under sections272, 420, 467, 468 and 471I.P.C. is unjustified. Learned A.G.A. opposed the prayer for bail but could not dispute the aforesaid facts as argued by learned counsel for the applicant.",
